  "notes": "Used for formal, institutional membership — not for casually joining a group of friends. The particle に marks what is being joined, and the particle に or への introduces the target.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜に{加入|かにゅう}する (to join ~)\n- 〜への{加入|かにゅう} (joining ~)\n- {加入|かにゅう}{者|しゃ} (member, subscriber)\n- {加入|かにゅう}{手続|てつづ}き (enrollment procedure)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {加入|かにゅう} — joining a group/plan/service (formal membership)\n- {入会|にゅうかい} — joining a club or association\n- {参加|さんか} — participating in an event or activity",
